===Membership===

Membership in the IFCB is open to national bodybuilding federations that meet the federation's governance and anti-doping standards. Each member federation is responsible for organizing national championships, selecting athletes for international competition, and enforcing IFCB regulations within its jurisdiction.

The IFCB's 142 member federations span all six inhabited continents. The largest federations by membership are the United Midlands Bodybuilding Federation (UMBBF), the Baliscan Confederation of Bodybuilding (BCB), the Okaiken Bodybuilding Association (OBA), and the Echian Federation of Bodybuilding (EFB).

==Competitions==

===Mr. Adonia===

{{main|Mr. Adonia}}

[[Mr. Adonia]] is the IFCB's flagship competition and the most prestigious title in professional bodybuilding. Held annually since 1965, the competition is the centrepiece of the Adonia Fitness & Performance Weekend, a three-day event that includes the Mr. Adonia Open division, Classic Physique, Men's Physique, 212 Division, and the female equivalents (Ms. Adonia, Fitness Adonia, Figure Adonia).

The competition is held at the Portsmith Grand Convention Center in [[Portsmith]], [[United Midlands]], with occasional international editions. The 1975 contest in [[Okami]], [[Okaiken]], was the first held outside the United Midlands.

===Ms. Adonia===

{{main|Ms. Adonia}}

[[Ms. Adonia]] is the female equivalent of Mr. Adonia, awarded to the winner of the professional women's bodybuilding contest at the Adonia Fitness & Performance Weekend. The competition was introduced in 1980, following the IFCB's expansion into women's bodybuilding. The first Ms. Adonia was [[Ingrid Hellström]] of [[Breisland]], who won three consecutive titles (1980–1982).

===Qualifying circuit===

The IFCB operates a global qualifying circuit for Mr. Adonia, collectively referred to as the Adonia Qualifying Season. The circuit runs for approximately one year, ending several months before the Mr. Adonia competition. Athletes earn qualification by placing in the top three at qualifying contests, winning a qualifying contest, or ranking among the top three in total points.

